<figure><img height="1732" sizes="(max-width: 1010px) calc(100vw - 60px), 690px" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tropical-beach-palm-trees-lava-rocks-blue-sky-6c.jpeg?ssl=1&amp;w=690&amp;quality=90 690w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tropical-beach-palm-trees-lava-rocks-blue-sky-6c.jpeg?ssl=1&amp;w=1035&amp;quality=90 1035w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tropical-beach-palm-trees-lava-rocks-blue-sky-6c.jpeg?ssl=1&amp;w=1380&amp;quality=90 1380w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tropical-beach-palm-trees-lava-rocks-blue-sky-6c.jpeg?ssl=1&amp;w=2070&amp;quality=90 2070w, https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tropical-beach-palm-trees-lava-rocks-blue-sky-6c.jpeg?ssl=1&amp;w=2760&amp;quality=90 2760w" width="2760" data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" src="https://i0.wp.com/sixcolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tropical-beach-palm-trees-lava-rocks-blue-sky-6c.jpeg?ssl=1&#038;w=1380&#038;quality=90" alt="A sunny tropical beach with golden sand, dark volcanic rocks, and turquoise water curving toward a point lined with palm trees and low buildings, beneath a deep blue sky with wispy white clouds." /><figcaption>I studied composers right here. (It didn&#8217;t help.)</figcaption></figure>
<p>It&#8217;s been a busy and incredibly weird year.</p>
<p>In January I <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/03/ill-take-beach-reading-for-1000-ken/">got the call to be on <em>Jeopardy!</em></a>, which turned a planned beach vacation into a seaside study session.<sup id="fnref-42535-wsj"><a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/thankful/#fn-42535-wsj" class="jetpack-footnote" title="Read footnote.">1</a></sup> We taped the show in February (I knew Jamie Ding when he was just a one-day champion!) and then it aired in March. I had a watch party at my house with a real this-is-your-life selection of guests, from long-ago coworkers to neighbors to the other people on my Sunday morning curling team.</p>
<p>Somewhere in there I went to New York for the <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/03/apple-introduces-colorful-macbook-neo-at-599/">MacBook Neo event</a> and ended up at one point chatting with John Ternus, Phil Schiller, and Greg Joswiak <a href="https://zeppelin.flights/@jsnell/116439930139479351">simultaneously</a>.</p>
<p>In April, <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/03/apple-at-50-for-further-reading/">Apple celebrated its 50th anniversary</a>. That led to an idea for a podcast, so in June, Myke Hurley and I put ourselves out there and <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/06/designed-in-california-help-up-bring-apple-history-to-life/">sought crowdfunding</a> for a new show about Apple history. To our legitimate shock, you showed up to support us at a level beyond our wildest dreams, which made <a href="https://designed.fm">Designed in California</a> a reality.</p>
<p>That project has required a frankly enormous amount of work, but it&#8217;s also been incredibly rewarding and I am very proud of the result. It&#8217;s fair to say that Myke and I both got a new job this summer, which has required some serious recalibration and optimization of some of our other projects, but it&#8217;s all good news. We love doing it and are so happy that you all helped give us the ability to fully commit to the project. (I am also learning an awful lot about Apple history and about how to manage large numbers of PDFs and transcripts when doing research!)</p>
<p>My youngest graduated from college, moved into an apartment with friends (with assistance and pizza from mom and dad), and got a job. There were several <a href="https://mwg.aaa.com/via/road-trips/electric-vehicle-bay-area-eugene">long drives up and down I-5</a> as a part of that. We went to a World Cup match. I wrote <a href="https://sixcolors.com/offsite/2026/08/jason-snells-productivity-picks/">something for the App Store</a>. I bought a Hawaiian shirt and <a href="https://www.theincomparable.com/magnum/127/">went to Magnum P.I. day</a> in Detroit.</p>
<p>The fall brought one of the busiest Apple product seasons in recent memory, as the company rolled out a new <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/10/iphone-18-pro-review-apples-priciest-pro-phone-ever-poses-a-challenge-for-upgraders/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> and a <em>really</em> new <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/10/iphone-duo-24-hours-in-the-splash-zone/">iPhone Duo</a>, a <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/macbook-pro-with-proled-review-you-could-even-say-it-glows/">touchscreen MacBook Pro</a>, a <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/homeview-review-a-late-arrival-with-promise-but-still-showing-some-seams/">home smart screen</a>, and a load of other <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/09/m6-mac-mini-review-tiny-pricey-and-powerful/">Mac</a> and <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/11/ipad-mini-review-a-modern-multitasker/">iPad</a> stuff, across many weeks. At one point I think I had three or four product-review embargoes lined up in a row.</p>
<p>Somewhere in there, in <em>very</em> late September, I went to Memphis and we did another <a href="https://sixcolors.com/link/2026/10/support-st-jude-and-watch-the-2026-relay-podcastathon-2/">12-hour podcast telethon</a> to benefit the mission of St. Jude.</p>
<p>Only now, after a delightful but poorly timed week of travel (I scheduled a trip to the east coast without realizing just how long the Apple product season was going to extend this year), is the dust beginning to clear. And here we are, at Thanksgiving, just the right time to begin reflecting on what we&#8217;ve all experienced and what we&#8217;re thankful for.</p>
<p>I am thankful for the amazing year I&#8217;ve had, and to everyone who made it possible, from my collaborators (at Six Colors, Relay, The Incomparable, and elsewhere) to the audiences of those various projects to my friends and family who have been understanding and supportive during the most interesting of times.</p>
<p>So: It&#8217;s been a busy and extremely weird year, and I wouldn&#8217;t change a thing. Thank you all.</p>
